msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:22
#: b40f00a95b7e49e797cb8e67397059d4
msgid "Set :ref:`ICE_ENABLE <ICE_ENABLE>` = 1 to enable the ICE feature (you may need to reload parameters after setting this in order to see below parameters)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:25
#: 77996fe35bd64c7c9f99800144d79ae8
msgid "Throttle Servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:26
#: e90be5fd552745fc8e640289f3d0c219
msgid "Throttle control for an IC engine is similar to controlling a standard brushless ESC. The throttle servo can be connected to any servo output with a :ref:`SERVOx_FUNCTION<SERVO3_FUNCTION>` set to 70 (Channel 3 is configured this way by default). It is important to set the Min and Max PWM values on this servo output to be within the mechanical limits of your throttle assembly (using :ref:`SERVOx_MIN<SERVO3_MIN>` and :ref:`SERVOx_MAX<SERVO3_MAX>`). While doing this, also verify that the servo moves in the correct direction with respect to manual throttle input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:28
#: e645321164b340959d1a51b39377c488
msgid "Note that, by default, the throttle servo will not move unless the vehicle is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:30
#: 2fdd62af541e48e2bf9d9e36c58b5827
msgid "Armed, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:31
#: 5432d307f9214a4fbda6074b7651a09b
msgid "The engine is considered \"running\" (start command received and RPM above threshold, or no RPM sensor configured)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:33
#: a3ca3ccd106e484d9fda03ebacf60e50
msgid "To test your throttle servo limits safely, you can set :ref:`ICE_OPTIONS<ICE_OPTIONS>` bit 2 (Value +4) to allow throttle control while disarmed in Manual mode, and it does not require the engine to be considered \"running\". If you do not want this option long-term, be sure to disable it after testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:35
#: 42e9924d745f46f5852afbf91b560f4c
msgid "For setting :ref:`SERVOx_MIN<SERVO3_MIN>`, you can either set it to the PWM value that corresponds to idle throttle, or set it to the PWM value that corresponds to fully closed throttle, allowing you to cut the engine even if you do not have and ignition switch. If you set it to the fully closed throttle, be sure to set :ref:`ICE_IDLE_PCT<ICE_IDLE_PCT>` to an appropriate value so that the engine does not stall after starting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:37
#: c6924be1f52144db8c4a9ffa2a29a22d
msgid "If you set :ref:`ICE_IDLE_PCT<ICE_IDLE_PCT>` to a value greater than zero, the engine will be allowed to start while disarmed. If you do not want this, set :ref:`ICE_OPTIONS<ICE_OPTIONS>` bit 3 (value +8) to prevent starting while disarmed. See `Controlling the Engine`_ below for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:39
#: 0334389421294229be6ab59e8ce9c10b
msgid "After configuring the limits of your throttle servo, the following parameters must be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:41
#: a70ada5a5a0c4fd292af4c463ef340cc
msgid "Set :ref:`THR_MIN <THR_MIN>` to the desired setting at idle. This will be found empirically during engine testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:42
#: ab478dc0493347e4acef5b1e3b802cc6
msgid "Set :ref:`THR_SLEWRATE <THR_SLEWRATE>` to a value appropriate for your engine. 20%/s is a good starting point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:43
#: 166c3f17d64c463bbba343131901379b
msgid "Set :ref:`THR_MAX <THR_MAX>` if you would like to prevent your engine from reaching full throttle."
msgstr ""

