#: c536171c8801423aa44b0f78f81ee468
msgid "``ICE_PWM_IGN_OFF`` is the PWM value sent to the ignition power switch when the engine should be stopped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:105
#: 637e0582580a4e6badef36c3522e93c3
msgid "RC Switch Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:107
#: 35314c0221f845588e201d443e753f1e
msgid "It is common to use a 3 position switch on an RC transmitter is used to control the engine. This switch has the following three positions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:109
#: 72e4ef3bce2c48ca9c052e959a084687
msgid "Low: Force the engine to be disabled. This ignores MAVLink commands and mission items that attempt to control the engine's state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:110
#: e6e33794f89a4cad9d3ca342b2a577a4
msgid "Mid: Keep the current state of the engine, but allow MAVLink commands and mission items to change the state of the engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:111
#: 22c9b639994d4c069b31b0012531db65
msgid "High: Force the engine to be enabled. This ignores MAVLink commands and mission items that attempt to control the engine's state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:113
#: 7b87e5c550244a969ce5c1a156efaabd
msgid "To start the engine, raise the switch to the high position. If you want the automatic engine-cut features to work, be sure to lower the switch to the middle position after the engine has started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:115
#: 8453e64e38e743078f8a31c8d807face
msgid "To stop the engine, lower the switch to the low position. If you want the engine to be automatically start with a mission, or want to use a MAVLink command to start the engine, be sure to raise the switch to the middle position after the engine has stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:117
#: 22d27435278f4ef3afd2f8444382ef6b
msgid "To configure the RC switch,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:122
#: 2d523aa5e53f49da8157613379ffee81
msgid "Set an RC auxiliary switch (:ref:`RCx_OPTION<RC6_OPTION>` = 179) be used to start the engine. This channel can start the engine or stop the engine via the ``Ignition`` and ``Starter`` motor/servo outputs (see :ref:`common-rcoutput-mapping`). Normally, the \"kill\" PWM value is anything below 1300us, but this can be changed using the :ref:`ICE_STARTCHN_MIN<ICE_STARTCHN_MIN>` parameter. Setting up this channel and its RC control is required for operation in order to provide a \"kill\" function on the throttle, even if there is no ignition or starter control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:126
#: 3ee6b0b8695b46edb43da8090e13f4ac
msgid "Set ``ICE_START_CHAN`` to the channel number corresponding to a switch on the transmitter which will be used to start the engine. This channel can start the engine or stop the engine via the ``Ignition`` and ``Starter`` outputs. Normally, the \"kill\" PWM value is anything below 1300us, but this can be changed using the :ref:`ICE_STARTCHN_MIN<ICE_STARTCHN_MIN>` parameter. Setting up this channel and its RC control is required for operation in order to provide a \"kill\" function on the throttle, even if there is no ignition or starter control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:128
#: 0824afbb84f84e419272c6901edca5a7
msgid "These parameters may also need to be adjusted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:130
#: 6ea587109e004cc6b9e40064c18146fc
msgid ":ref:`ICE_STARTCHN_MIN<ICE_STARTCHN_MIN>` is the minimum PWM below which the start channel input will be ignored. This is a safety feature to prevent bad RC input from stopping the motor while the aircraft is beyond line of sight, if the RC protocol is incorrectly configured. Default is zero, meaning disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:133
#: 89d8514976b643819e76d3e36890d423
msgid "Starting with an Onboard Starter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:134
#: cb2bd9d14c664f46bf4fca7d6458c6b0
msgid "If using an onboard starter, it is strongly recommended to configure an RPM sensor for the engine, since the primary benefit of an onboard starter is to automatically attempt to restart the engine if it fails in flight. See `RPM Configuration`_ below for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:136
#: d277637595f142aa9176abaa066eba09
msgid "The auto-start functionality will attempt to start the engine any time the vehicle is armed, the engine is enabled, and the measured RPM is below the :ref:`ICE_RPM_THRESH <ICE_RPM_THRESH>`. If the engine is not successfully started within a configurable amount of time, the program will wait for a configurable delay before attempting to start again. It is important to remember that the starter will run in pulses. DO NOT approach the engine between failed start attempts as the starter will attempt to start again if the engine is still enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:138
#: 5fe3d3b30ffd4c2c9b66a89d31f60d7a
msgid ":ref:`ICE_START_PCT <ICE_START_PCT>` overrides the throttle setting during start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:139
#: a99b7c2dfa004c8da1ab21b1458a80e6
msgid ":ref:`ICE_STARTER_TIME <ICE_STARTER_TIME>` controls the maximum amount of time the starter will run in each start attempt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:140
#: 06dead5157784ae09e75d6943fbaacdc
msgid ":ref:`ICE_START_DELAY <ICE_START_DELAY>` sets a delay between start attempts. This can be useful when your starter has a limited duty cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:141
#: 91cec17f5e694d2e939c483ecdd39e86
msgid ":ref:`ICE_RPM_THRESH <ICE_RPM_THRESH>` sets the minimum RPM reading for the engine to be considered running. This should be set to a value below your idle RPM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:142
#: 9ef0e03d829b403e85cd13eb2f4deb6a
msgid ":ref:`ICE_STRT_MX_RTRY<ICE_STRT_MX_RTRY>` if set to a value greater than 0 then the engine will retry starting the engine this many times before giving up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:146
#: 158fe1e290c6460184d5855574e9c397
msgid "Starting without an Onboard Starter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:147
#: bfff551a7ff84dc0a4f406e367d86e76
msgid "If using a hand-held starter motor to start the engine, set :ref:`ICE_STARTER_TIME <ICE_STARTER_TIME>` to a relatively high value (at least 10 seconds). This will give you time between hitting the switch and starting the engine with the hand-held starter. After this time period has elapsed, the throttle will drop from :ref:`ICE_START_PCT <ICE_START_PCT>` to :ref:`ICE_IDLE_PCT <ICE_IDLE_PCT>` regardless of whether the engine has started or not. *After* this point, if you are using an optional RPM sensor, the engine start logic may begin again if the engine has not started, or if it stalls after starting and the RPM drops below the :ref:`ICE_RPM_THRESH <ICE_RPM_THRESH>`. Because of this, it is not recommended to set a short time period for the starter cycle, since it will periodically dip the throttle as you are trying to start the engine, which might make it harder to start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:149
#: ab2a53bc73de43f993a74dc1abed90d3
msgid "If the engine stalls after startup, toggle the engine control off and on, then try to start again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:152
#: e5c7a50569284181ad8048b4e0cf086c
msgid "RPM Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:153
#: 90ed6e745a7f46a3bbcde11b9f829f44
msgid "ArduPilot supports generic pulse tachometers connected to GPIO pins (such as the Aux servo pins on a PixHawk or Cube). A tachometer may be made using a simple hall effect switch IC. Some ignition modules support a tachometer output that can be connected directly to the GPIO pins. Desert Aircraft Electronic Ignition V2 modules support tachometer output on the signal pin of the power input connector. Note that when connecting an RPM sensor to an AUX pin, it is important to make sure that this pin is not configured to output a PWM value and, instead, be a GPIO pin. See :ref:`common-gpios` and :ref:`common-rpm` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:155
#: bdc07a66b5ad43c394dbe2a14157814a
msgid "Alternatively, many electronic fuel injection (EFI) systems transmit engine RPM via their own telemetry system. If you have configured an EFI system, and it supports RPM telemetry, then ArduPilot can use this RPM value directly without needing a separate RPM sensor. See :ref:`Electronic Fuel Injection <common-efi>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:157
#: ec17a49d9425477a81caab2391d074b7
msgid "In order to configure an RPM sensor, the following parameters must be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:159
#: e50a3332a7644d8797c8a4743509606f
msgid "Set :ref:`RPM1_TYPE <RPM1_TYPE>` for whichever RPM source you are using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:160
#: 351c68046e79453983b8d3f43fbaceb4
msgid "Set the remaining 'RPM_*' parameters as appropriate for your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:161
#: be29e9612edd4518b93060b1eae16be9
msgid "Set :ref:`ICE_RPM_CHAN <ICE_RPM_CHAN>` to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:164
#: 864f81f0062f44d3945ff670aa37da76
msgid "Idle and redline governors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:166
#: 53fb96b5ad434458acca80e7c0d7c224
msgid "These features rely on having a source for engine RPM. See `RPM Configuration`_ above for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:168
#: 567097f6077740eebe64421f5b788274
msgid "The idle governor allows the autopilot to adjust the throttle to maintain an RPM value when the commanded throttle is low. This can be useful when the engine is waiting for takeoff and reduces the workload on the pilot during that time. Increasing the throttle command will give the expected throttle response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:170
#: e855fd8b420d4dce8ab484d672edd982
msgid "Prior to ArduPilot 4.7, while the aircraft is disarmed, the idle governor only works in Manual mode (and only if :ref:`ICE_OPTIONS<ICE_OPTIONS>` bit 2 is set). If your engine cannot run reliably without the idle governor, you will need to arm in Manual mode before switching to another mode to take off. Once armed, the idle governor will work in all modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:172
#: eac8f1e68c7c4a9c923422fcd448cefe
msgid ":ref:`ICE_IDLE_PCT<ICE_IDLE_PCT>` This is the minimum percentage throttle output while running, this includes being disarmed, but not while outputs are disabled by the safety switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:173
#: b067e1a066ba42b889e3ba1e8db8b28d
msgid ":ref:`ICE_IDLE_RPM<ICE_IDLE_RPM>` This configures the RPM that will be commanded by the idle governor. Set to -1 to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:174
#: befe74a247ba4cd7bc508dcf389f56c2
msgid ":ref:`ICE_IDLE_DB<ICE_IDLE_DB>` This configures the RPM deadband that is tolerated before adjusting the idle setpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:175
#: ce61e69771474586980b321ece66cc06
msgid ":ref:`ICE_IDLE_SLEW<ICE_IDLE_SLEW>` This configures the slewrate used to adjust the idle setpoint in percentage points per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:177
#: 95f68b8fe40f40509145a1d37fee9e1e
msgid "The redline governor will slowly reduce the throttle if the RPM remains above the given RPM value. Generally, this RPM value is provided by the manufacturer of the engine. If the commanded throttle drops faster or lower than the point the governor started, then the governor will be released and normal control of the throttle will return to normal throttle response. A warning message will appear on the GCS. Setting :ref:`ICE_OPTIONS<ICE_OPTIONS>` bit 1 allows disabling the throttle actions of the redline governor, but still displays the GCS warning message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:179
#: 20e21cd1d5a942d4b9346bd5ca1c2fae
msgid ":ref:`ICE_REDLINE_RPM<ICE_REDLINE_RPM>` Maximum RPM for the engine provided by the manufacturer. A value of 0 disables this feature."
msgstr ""

