#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:197
#: a73c98f5abb041dd99a3898a57e874f5
msgid "Vibration isolation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:199
#: 9df47605844a40f28bcd0cf4699ac18e
msgid "The high vibration from internal combustion engines means that :ref:`vibration dampening <common-vibration-damping>` is critical.  It is often necessary to mount the autopilot on a plate with `self-adhesive lead weights <https://www.amazon.com/Great-Planes-Segmented-Weights-6-Ounce/dp/B0015KLJE0>`__ added to increase its mass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:203
#: 43e723d2dd5e438f831a0d286608badd
msgid "When using Internal Combustion Engine (ICE) motors, vibration during engine run-up can cause the IMU consistency checks to fail, preventing arming. In ArduPilot 4.7 and later an option has been added to :ref:`ARMING_OPTIONS<ARMING_OPTIONS>`: bit 2 (Skip IMU consistency checks when ICE motor running)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ice.rst:208
#: bbdacd3f74b74ece96bacb8e972fcbd1
msgid "When this bit is set (value +4), ArduPilot will bypass the IMU consistency check if an ICE motor is running. This is intended for setups where ICE engines are typically started before arming, and their vibration may otherwise trigger false failures."
msgstr ""
